  "name": "Yueju (Shaoxing / Shanghai opera)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Yueju Shaoxing opera, a Chinese regional opera tradition originating in the rural Sheng County of Zhejiang province at the turn of the twentieth century and crystallizing in 1920s-1930s Shanghai as an all-female-cast operatic form (yueju is one of only a handful of Chinese operas traditionally performed exclusively by female actors playing both male and female roles). Distinguished from kunqu and jingju by its lyrical, romance-focused dramaturgical orientation, accessible Wu-dialect Shaoxing-area linguistic register, and the all-female casting convention. The 1953 film adaptation of the canonical Liang Shanbo and Zhu Yingtai butterfly-lovers legend (with Yuan Xuefen and Fan Ruijuan in the principal roles) consolidated the national audience.",
